JL — https://github.com/rampaa/JL
Apache License 2.0. Full text in third_party/JL/LICENSE.

Ported from https://github.com/rampaa/JL/tree/85ae02eeb84f378387f48c12e7b468390a9f2007:

  src/jp/            JL.Core/Japanese/JapaneseUtils.cs — the text normalization, the
                     classification predicates and the chōonpu variants. src/jp/japanesetables.h
                     is generated from the same file by tools/gen-jp-tables.py.
  src/deconj/        JL.Core/Deconjugation/{Deconjugator,DeconjugatorUtils,Rule,VirtualRule,
                     Form,ProcessNode}.cs and JL.Core/Lookup/{RuleBucket,LookupResultUtils}.cs.
                     data/deconjugation_rules.json is a copy of
                     JL.Core/Resources/deconjugation_rules.json.
  src/dict/          the format loaders under JL.Core/Dicts/** (JMdict, JMnedict, KANJIDIC2,
                     Yomichan term, kanji, pitch-accent and frequency banks, the custom word and
                     name lists), JL.Core/WordClass/JmdictWordClassUtils.cs for the
                     part-of-speech table, and JL.Core/Utilities/ResourceUpdater.cs for the
                     conditional-GET update protocol.
  src/lookup/        JL.Core/Lookup/LookupUtils.cs for the pipeline and the part-of-speech gate,
                     JL.Core/Lookup/LookupResult.cs CompareTo for the fourteen-criterion result
                     comparator, and the frequency and pitch-accent resolution order.

Each ported file names the JL file it comes from in its own header comment.
tests/deconj/deconjugation_cases.h is generated from JL.Core.Tests/Deconjugation.
tests/data/dict/MockJMdict.xml is copied from JL.Core.Tests/Resources; its underlying
JMdict dictionary material retains the EDRDG attribution and terms described below.

